      "content": "i mean, if the causal link isn't even clear, then why are so many companies still doubling down on these massive DEI budgets? it seems like even if the data is \"nuanced,\" the actual implementation often feels more like a way to check boxes for public image than anything that actually helps the business. don't you think the push for these programs is more about social momentum than actual business logic at this point?",
